> > > This isnt a bug on our end, this is a ratelimit they are choosing to enforce based on what client ur using
> > > no action item for us
> > 
> > 
> > i thing its bug, coz i need edit config file for working in "Kimi For Coding". It seems like I should either remove this provider from the list in OpenCode or replace User-Agent with Kimi KLI by default. Because without manually adding it to the configuration, it simply won't work. Here's what I added to the configuration to get it working without limits again:
> > ```
> > "kimi-for-coding": {
> >   "models": {
> >     "k2p6": {
> >       "headers": {
> >         "User-Agent": "KimiCLI/1.5"
> >       }
> >     }
> >   }
> > }
> > ```
> 
> which config, and how to add it. please give an example.

just add this code to your config file /Users/xxxxxx/.config/opencode/opencode.json (or opencode.jsonс)

ex:

```
{
  "$schema": "https://opencode.ai/config.json",
  "default_agent": "Ask",
  "provider": {
    "deepseek_v4": {
      "name": "DeepSeek v4",
      "npm": "@ai-sdk/openai-compatible",
      "options": {
        "baseURL": "https://api.deepseek.com"
      },
      "models": {
        "deepseek-v4-flash": {
          "name": "DeepSeek V4 Flash"
        },
        "deepseek-v4-pro": {
          "name": "DeepSeek V4 Pro"
        }
      }
    },
    "kimi-for-coding": {
      "models": {
        "k2p6": {
          "headers": {
            "User-Agent": "KimiCLI/1.5"
          }
        }
      }
    }
  }
}
```
